# Ballad of the Chain

**(Verse 1)**
Two thousand eight, the markets fell apart,
A whitepaper landed, a fresh and quiet start.
Nine pages of a vision no banker could ignore,
A peer-to-peer answer to the rot inside the core.
No name behind the curtain, just Satoshi on the page,
A genesis block burning like a beacon through the age.
"Chancellor on the brink," the headline locked inside,
A timestamp in the ledger that the truth could never hide.

**(Chorus)**
Run the nodes, hum the proof of work,
Every block a promise where the doubters lurk.
No king, no vault, no middleman to blame,
Just math and light and the ballad of the chain.
Hodl through the winter, hodl through the rain,
We are running on the rhythm of the ballad of the chain.

**(Verse 2)**
The miners spin their engines, hashing through the night,
A trillion little guesses chasing one byte just right.
Difficulty rising like a tide against the shore,
Ten minutes between heartbeats, never less and never more.
Halving comes in seasons, cutting the reward,
Scarcity is sharpened like the edge upon a sword.
Twenty-one million, that's the ceiling and the law,
No printer in the basement, no exception, not a flaw.

**(Chorus)**
Run the nodes, hum the proof of work,
Every block a promise where the doubters lurk.
No king, no vault, no middleman to blame,
Just math and light and the ballad of the chain.
Hodl through the winter, hodl through the rain,
We are running on the rhythm of the ballad of the chain.

**(Bridge)**
They called it just a bubble, they called it just a fad,
They laughed at every pizza for the fortune that it had.
But the network never sleeps and the ledger never lies,
Ten thousand watching keepers under twice ten thousand eyes.
Keys inside your pocket, your kingdom and your gate,
Not your keys, not your coins — that's the lesson, learn it straight.

**(Verse 3)**
From Lightning bolts of payment to the cold and quiet store,
A wallet on a mountain or a phone outside the door.
A currency for everyone who never had a bank,
A signal in the static that the powerful can't outrank.
So let the candles flicker, green and red they sway,
The chain rolls ever forward, block by block, each day.

**(Final Chorus)**
Run the nodes, hum the proof of work,
Every block a promise where the doubters lurk.
No king, no vault, no middleman to blame,
Just math and light and the ballad of the chain.
Hodl through the winter, hodl through the rain,
Forever in the rhythm of the ballad of the chain.